{"id": "185128", "name": "הרכבת פונקציה עם מסילות – התאמת נוסחת ההרכבה לציור המסילה (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "functions": [{"name": "x1", "params": ["t"], "body": "x1"}, {"name": "y1", "params": ["t"], "body": "y1"}, {"name": "x2", "params": ["t"], "body": "x2"}, {"name": "y2", "params": ["t"], "body": "y2"}, {"name": "x3", "params": ["t"], "body": "x3"}, {"name": "y3", "params": ["t"], "body": "y3"}], "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Let \\(f(x,y)={{CT:0}}\\)</p><p>Consider three functions \\(\\alpha_i: [a,b] \\rightarrow R^2\\) from an interval inside the real line to the plane. The resulting paths in the plane are depicted below.</p><p>Each function \\(g_i = f \\circ \\alpha_i: [a,b] \\rightarrow R\\) is a composition of \\(f(x,y)\\) with one of these paths. Match each function with the graph of the corresponding path.</p><div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center;gap:12px\"><div style=\"flex:0 1 360px;text-align:center\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:4px\">path 1:</div>{{CT:1}}</div><div style=\"flex:0 1 360px;text-align:center\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:4px\">path 2:</div>{{CT:2}}</div><div style=\"flex:0 1 360px;text-align:center\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:4px\">path 3:</div>{{CT:3}}</div></div></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><p>(Please answer with 1, 2 or 3)</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(g_1(t)={{CT:4}}\\) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Path number: [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:8px\"></div><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(g_2(t)={{CT:5}}\\) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Path number: [[input:ans2]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans2]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:8px\"></div><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(g_3(t)={{CT:6}}\\) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Path number: [[input:ans3]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans3]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> \\(f(x,y)=x^2+y^2\\) is the squared distance of the point \\((x,y)\\) from the origin, so \\(g(t)=f(\\alpha(t))\\) is the squared distance of the moving point \\(\\alpha(t)\\) from the origin. Read from each picture how this distance behaves, and compare with the formulas.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — The composition with each path</b><br><ul><li><b>Path 1</b> is the unit circle \\(\\alpha(t)=(\\cos t,\\sin t)\\): every point is at distance 1 from the origin, so <p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ f(\\cos t,\\sin t)={{CT:7}}=1 \\]</p>is <b>constant</b>.</li><li><b>Path 2</b> is the parabola \\(\\alpha(t)=(3t,t^2)\\) (the points satisfy \\(y=x^2/9\\)), which goes off to infinity, so the distance is unbounded:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ f(3t,t^2)={{CT:8}} \\]</p>a polynomial in \\(t\\), equal to 0 only at \\(t=0\\) and growing without bound.</li><li><b>Path 3</b> is the ellipse \\(\\alpha(t)=(5\\sin t,2\\cos t)\\) (the points satisfy \\(\\frac{x^2}{25}+\\frac{y^2}{4}=1\\)): the distance changes between 2 and 5, so<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ f(5\\sin t,2\\cos t)={{CT:9}} \\]</p>is periodic and oscillates between \\(4\\) and \\(25\\).</li></ul></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — The matching</b><br>Compare each of your functions with these three types:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\(g_1(t)={{CT:4}}\\ \\longrightarrow\\ \\text{Path }{{CT:10}}\\)</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\(g_2(t)={{CT:5}}\\ \\longrightarrow\\ \\text{Path }{{CT:11}}\\)</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\(g_3(t)={{CT:6}}\\ \\longrightarrow\\ \\text{Path }{{CT:12}}\\)</p>Hence<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ g_1:\\ {{CT:10}},\\qquad g_2:\\ {{CT:11}},\\qquad g_3:\\ {{CT:12}} \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:prt1]]<br />[[feedback:prt2]]<br />[[feedback:prt3]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p>Correct answer, well done.</p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p>Your answer is partially correct.</p>", "prtincorrect": "<p>Incorrect answer.</p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans2", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans3", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "sol1", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt1-1-T", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The first match is correct.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt1-1-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The first match is incorrect, {{CT:13}} is the correct path.</div>"}}]}, {"name": "prt2", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans2", "tans": "sol2", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-1-T", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The second match is correct.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-1-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The second match is incorrect, {{CT:14}} is the correct path.</div>"}}]}, {"name": "prt3", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans3", "tans": "sol3", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt3-1-T", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The third match is correct.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt3-1-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The third match is incorrect, {{CT:15}} is the correct path.</div>"}}]}], "qvnames": ["comp_lst", "f", "f1", "f11", "f2", "f22", "f3", "f33", "g1", "g2", "g3", "sol1", "sol2", "sol3", "x1", "x2", "x3", "y1", "y2", "y3"], "nvariants": 6}